    <bpmn:process id="W_W1946" name="W1946. Consignment Agreement Renewal &amp; Terms Negotiation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Consignment agreement expiration (typically annual)
Frequency: ~15–25 renewals/year
Volume: ~15–25 active consignment vendors
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, VP Merchandising, VP Supply Chain, CFO, Vendor
Source: workflow W1946 — Consignment Agreement Renewal &amp; Terms Negotiation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1946_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1946_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1946_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1946_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1946_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1946_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1946_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1946_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1946_Start4" name="Consignment agreement expiration (typically annual)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1946_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1946_Task5" name="Category Manager prepares renewal analysis: (a) past year performance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Category Manager prepares renewal analysis: (a) past year performance: sell-through rate, margin, return rate, (b) compare consignment arrangement vs. direct purchase alternative, (c) vendor relationship: payment timeliness, dispute resolution, support quality, (d) market conditions: are there alternative vendors offering better consignment terms?
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1946_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1946_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1946_Task6" name="Negotiation: (a) improved consignment cost (target 2–5% reduction annually)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Negotiation: (a) improved consignment cost (target 2–5% reduction annually), (b) expanded SKU range (add high-demand items to consignment), (c) improved terms: faster settlement, better damage responsibility allocation, (d) performance incentives: volume-based consignment cost reduction
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per negotiation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1946_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1946_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1946_Task7" name="CFO approves consignment terms from financial perspective: (a) margin impact…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CFO approves consignment terms from financial perspective: (a) margin impact, (b) balance sheet impact (consignment stock is off-balance-sheet — vendor-owned), (c) settlement terms cash flow impact
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1946_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1946_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1946_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
