    <bpmn:process id="W_W1947" name="W1947. VMI-to-Standard Procurement Conversion Decision" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: VMI vendor consistently underperforming; strategic decision to internalize replenishment
Frequency: ~1–2 conversion decisions/year
Volume: 12 VMI vendors monitored
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: VP Supply Chain, Category Manager, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1947 — VMI-to-Standard Procurement Conversion Decision</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1947_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1947_Lane1" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1947_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1947_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1947_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1947_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1947_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1947_Start3" name="VMI vendor consistently underperforming; strategic decision to internalize replenishment">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1947_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1947_Task4" name="VP Supply Chain identifies VMI vendor for conversion: (a) fill rate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Supply Chain identifies VMI vendor for conversion: (a) fill rate consistently &lt; 93% (below 97% target for 2+ quarters), (b) stockout frequency impacting sales, (c) vendor unable or unwilling to improve, (d) internal replenishment capability available (Buyer capacity, demand planning tools)
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1947_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1947_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1947_Task5" name="Decision analysis: (a) cost of conversion: additional Buyer labor, demand…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Decision analysis: (a) cost of conversion: additional Buyer labor, demand planning tool cost, (b) benefit of conversion: better fill rate, lower stockout, more control over replenishment timing, (c) risk of conversion: loss of vendor collaboration, BuildRight bears forecasting risk, (d) present business case to VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1947_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1947_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1947_Task6" name="If approved: (a) transition VMI SKUs to standard procurement per W2A, (b)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If approved: (a) transition VMI SKUs to standard procurement per W2A, (b) establish ROP/EOQ parameters per W312, (c) notify vendor of VMI termination per contractual notice period, (d) monitor first 90 days closely for service level impact
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 weeks transition</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1947_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1947_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1947_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1947_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-378 (ensure controlled execution — Consignment &amp; VMI Settlement &amp; Analytics (PA-45.3).) | - operational: VP Supply Chain review and approval gate
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
